# Build context hygiene for backend/Dockerfile.
#
# Two jobs. The obvious one is speed: `target/` alone is hundreds of megabytes and would be
# uploaded to the daemon on every build. The one that matters more is that nothing outside
# `pom.xml` and `src/` can reach the image — `qa-tmp/` in particular holds live QA JWTs
# (see backend/.gitignore), and a build context is not a place to discover that late.

target/

### QA scratch — payloads, tokens, captured output. Never in an image. ###
qa-tmp/
qa-tmp-*/

### Local-disk storage from pronto.storage.mode=local. Production runs mode=s3. ###
data/

### Environment files. Production configuration is injected by the ECS task definition. ###
.env
.env.*

### Editor / OS / VCS ###
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
.DS_Store
.git/
.gitignore

### Docs and build metadata that do not belong in a build context ###
**/README.md
HELP.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
